  "notes": "With the Lean rank-7 witness bounds/N-m4-upper-7.json this moves the cell to 6 <= chi(N^4) <= 7; there is no rank-6 witness. The argument (docs/notes/qutrit_m4_rank5_exclusion.md, section 2) depends on: (1) Fact A, that every one-qutrit slice of a rank-5 decomposition of |N>^4 has all five terms nonzero: chi(N^3) = 4 (bounds/N-m3-lower-4.json), the unique rank-4 decomposition of |N>^3 (research/constructions/data/N_m3_rank4.json), and the 0 lifts of case [A] of research/constructions/relaxed_lift.py at R = 5, declared here and not re-run. (2) Fact B of PR #86 (research/constructions/two_qutrit_slice.py, 431 s of tables for N, not re-run): no two-qutrit slice point of a rank-5 decomposition has exactly three nonzero terms. (3) The base-point argument of the note, section 2: every term is a nine-slice term or a diagonal line term along qutrits 1, 2, at most one term is a line term, every diagonal line meets the orbit {00, 01, 10, 11} of (0, 0) under the swap 0 <-> 1 of |N> on qutrits 1, 2 and the swap of those qutrits, so one base point per cover suffices. (4) The two-qutrit slice structure lemma of PR #86, which makes the matcher's option sets exhaustive; the matcher allows every flat through x_0 and does not use Facts A and B. (5) Exactness: all amplitudes lie in Q(zeta_12), and 65521 and 2013265921 are 1 mod 12, so the modular kernels list supersets of the true covers and matches, and every candidate cover and every hit is re-decided mod 2013265921 and in floating point (research/qutrit_m4_rank5/common.decide_terms), stored hits again by the aggregate. (6) The controls (note, section 5; research/qutrit_m4_rank5/results/N/control_*.json): the census's full 3-covers and 4-covers of |N>^2 against the stored rank-3 list and slice_lift.all_decompositions; planted five-term decompositions with generic, diagonal-line, dependent and repeated bases recovered; the rank-4 decomposition of |N>^3 recovered by 2 + 1 slicing; the rank-7 Lean witness recovered from its all-visible base points with the matcher at rank 7. Everything runs in the Python reference; there is no compiled kernel. Attested rather than reproduced because no certificate budget re-runs the full enumeration."
